-- title:
--   Tate curve: toric generators give a Γ₀(p^k)-structure
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, $p$ a prime, $k$ a natural number, $\zeta \in F$ a primitive $p^k$-th root of unity, and $n \ge 1$. Work over the Weierstrass curve [`ModularCurve.tateBase F n`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L46), i.e. the Tate curve [`ModularCurve.tateLaurent F`](def/ModularCurve_TateFormal.html#L86) over the Laurent series field $F(\!(q)\!)$ with coefficients pushed forward along the ring homomorphism [`ModularCurve.qExpand F n`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), which multiplies all exponents by $n$ (so $q \mapsto q^n$). For $c \in F$ let $(x(c), y(c)) =$ [`ModularCurve.toricPoint F n c`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L125) be the pair of Laurent series whose power-series coefficients are given by the explicit $q$-expansion formulas of the toric point with parameter $c$ at level $n$: the constant terms $c/(1-c)^2$ and $c^2/(1-c)^3$, and for $m \ge 1$ the divisor sums $\sum_{d \mid m,\ n \mid d} (m/d)\bigl(c^{m/d} + c^{-m/d}\bigr) - 2\,[n \mid m]\,\sigma_1(m/n)$ and $\sum_{d \mid m,\ n \mid d}\bigl(\binom{m/d}{2} c^{m/d} - \binom{m/d+1}{2} c^{-m/d}\bigr) + [n \mid m]\,\sigma_1(m/n)$. The assertion is that the monic polynomial $h = \prod_{1 \le a \le p^k/2,\ p \nmid a} \bigl(X - x(\zeta^a)\bigr)$ satisfies [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) for `tateBase F n` at $(p,k)$: when $p^k = 2$ this means $\deg h \le 1$, the coefficient of $X$ in $h$ equals $1$, and $h$ divides $\Psi_2^2$ of the curve; otherwise it means $\deg h \le \varphi(p^k)/2$, the coefficient of $X^{\varphi(p^k)/2}$ in $h$ equals $1$, the product $h \cdot \mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}$ divides $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k}}$, and $h$ divides `smulNumerator` $a$ $(\varphi(p^k)/2)$ $h$ for every $a$ with $2 \le a \le (p^k-1)/2$ and $p \nmid a$.
--
--   This is the cusp case of a $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-structure: on the Tate curve the cyclic subgroup of order $p^k$ generated by a toric point $\zeta$ is recorded by the polynomial whose roots are the abscissae of its generators up to sign. It feeds [`ModularCurve.exists_isGamma0PowAt_tateBase_and_map_coeffMap_eq_prod_X_sub_C_toricPoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isGamma0PowAt_tateBase_and_map_coeffMap_eq_prod_X_sub_C_toricPoint), which exhibits such a structure together with its behaviour under coefficient maps.
